Track 1: The Dixcove Demarcation
- Story & Context: When tropical squalls knocked out the coastal power line in June 1982, broadcast engineer Kofi Mensah hot-wired his pirate transmitter directly to the lightning rod atop an abandoned customs depot near Dixcove. As the smell of copper-sweet ozone filled the damp room, the band kicked into a galloping 6/8 horn fanfare to keep their valve oil from seizing in the ocean dampness, broadcasting their clandestine signal across the territorial waters just minutes ahead of municipal inspection jeeps. Lead vocalist Akua shouted the station's joyful call-sign into a corroded ribbon microphone: "When the sky splits open, our borders blow away!" The broadcast ended when a lightning strike fused the master mixer's faders into solid slag, but every battery-operated radio between Sekondi and Axim captured the euphoric birth of the sound.
