Track 2: "Who Told You the Border Was Dry?"
- Story & Context: Valve trombonist Ebo "Brass-Eye" Cudjoe tracked his most personal contribution inside a salt-damp wooden dory shed, nursing bruised knuckles from a scuffle with border patrollers over smuggled brass instruments. The room reeked of cedar shavings and paraffin lanterns while a looping ambient synthesizer reproduced the low, whistling pressure of the storm outside, contrasting Ebo’s heart-heavy confession with bounding, sunlit guitar licks. He wept between takes over the political boundaries separating his family across the Tano River, yet his horn countermelodies surged with unstoppable, bouncy defiance. Over a soaring, major-key brass crescendo, his cracked voice floated across the tape deck: "You measured the river, but the cloud belongs to me!" By the time the clouds parted and the pirate frequency faded to air hiss, Ebo's tearful lament had become the region's favorite wedding dance.
